Z||000000||AEmedic||12-18-2001||08:02 PM||||I am at the beginning stages of the "conversion decision". I am<BR>considering getting a complete engine assembly out of a salvage yard.<BR>Possibly from a late 80's early 90's Vette, Pont, etc. so that I can get<BR>the TPI, computer, wiring harness, etc together with the engine. Is this a<BR>good idea(cost) or should I build the engine and gather the TPI and other pieces from other<BR>sources. All this precedes the purchase of Archie's kit, since I am saving<BR>for<BR>the complete kit. Any advice is deeply appreciated.<BR>I also am having a problem with the brakes of my car. They intermitantly<BR>lock up in the front and the pedal gets very stiff, I also notice that the<BR>cruise stopped working. I took the caliper off the right and checked the<BR>pins and they were great, but I cleaned them up and lubed them. While it<BR>was apart I had a very hard time compressing the pistons??? Once I put it<BR>back together I took it for a drive and both front calipers locked up and<BR>were dragging till they smoked, then all at once they let go. I am not<BR>sure of the problem.<BR>Thanks for any help you can give,<BR>Chris Rogers<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Daleford||12-19-2001||08:08 AM||||AE    Don't know why you never got any advice on this,.... so I'll give mine.  I would get it all at once. If your picking up the engine at a salvage yard then they will have ECM, wiring,and everything there.  Not only will it all match, but it will cost less. I went one step further and got the whole car! [damaged body with the remaining bodypanels already picked over]  Only difference, I got a 4.9 powered Cadillac Deville. $500 for all and I don't have to buy an adapter kit! <P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTDude||12-19-2001||08:39 AM||||As far as the brakes go...sounds like bad brake hoses, or possibly calipers.  Remove the hose or loosen the bleeder and see if the  caliper will move in easy.  If so it's the brake hoses....if not it's the calipers.  Good luck!<P>phil pettus<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DSCF0003a_3.JPG"> <P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||1
